<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every sound this app rings is addressed by NAME at runtime, never through a
  compile-time R.raw reference: Capacitor's channel builder resolves
  `sound: 'msg_bell'` into `android.resource://<pkg>/raw/msg_bell` purely from
  the string. The resource shrinker sees only compile-time references, so
  without this file it strips whichever sound no Java/Kotlin line mentions —
  and the channel still arms and "rings" against a Uri that resolves to nothing.

  That failure is silent in both senses. The reminder picker keeps working,
  because its preview plays from assets/public/audio/, which shrinkResources
  never touches — so the choice looks saved while the notification that arrives
  wears the default chime instead of it. Only the notification itself tells you.

  Hence every name here:
    adhan_*  — the prayer voices (also passed as plain file names)
    iqama_*  — the جماعة's own recordings: the full iqamah, the mosque fragment,
               and the quiet chime, all addressed by name the same way
    msg_*    — the four «رنين» reminder tones behind صوت التنبيه
    notification — the app's own chime: the default tone, and the tap the
                   iqamah falls back to when «أذان الإقامة» is switched off

  tools:keep pins them regardless of how minify/shrink evolves; a sound added
  later must be listed here too or it will not survive packaging.
-->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@raw/adhan_*,@raw/msg_*,@raw/iqama*,@raw/notification" />
